; The tool project's own copy_files# of the err_trace submodule sources.
;
; This is NOT a second checkout and not a duplicated source: it copies the same
; two files asm/vendor/err_trace_local copies, from the same submodule, at build
; time. The submodule count stays at one and err.ml has exactly one source of
; truth in the repository.
;
; The stanza is repeated rather than shared because sharing is precisely what
; the project boundary forbids: a library lives in one project, and whichever
; project owned it, the other could not name it. Six lines is the price of the
; boundary.
;
; Reaching ../../../vendor/err_trace/src/ works because this project is nested
; inside the asm/ WORKSPACE even though it is a separate PROJECT. A root at
; tools/ocaml/ could not do this - the sources would lie outside its workspace.
;
; `wrapped false` is upstream's own setting and is what makes the module `Err`
; rather than `Err_trace.Err`, matching asm/'s spelling exactly.
;
; No enabled_if: unlike asm/vendor/err_trace_local, this copy is not disabled
; under Melange, because nothing here builds to JavaScript.

(copy_files#
 (files ../../../vendor/err_trace/src/err.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files ../../../vendor/err_trace/src/err.mli))

(library
 (name err_trace)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes byte native))
